* Example StarRC (StarXtract) command file for coupling-preserved SPEF extraction.
* This is the single-corner shape auto-generated by the run scripts; absolute
* site paths are replaced with <PLACEHOLDER> tokens. Fill them with your own
* ICC2 output / PDK paths (nothing here ships an actual PDK).
*
* Coupling recipe (the part that matters for crosstalk/SI):
*   EXTRACTION: RC
*   COUPLE_TO_GROUND: NO
*   COUPLING_ABS_THRESHOLD / REL_THRESHOLD: 0  (retain all coupling caps)

BLOCK: <TOP_MODULE>                          ; e.g. BoomCore
NDM_DATABASE: <ICC2_NDM_LIB>                 ; ICC2 place-and-route result library
MAPPING_FILE: <PDK_ROOT>/<layer_map_file>    ; e.g. saed14nm_1p9m_ndm_layer.map
CORNERS_FILE: <PDK_ROOT>/<corners_file>      ; BEOL RC/temperature corner definitions
SELECTED_CORNERS: Cnom_model_25              ; one corner: <RC>_model_<temp>
SIMULTANEOUS_MULTI_CORNER: NO
STAR_DIRECTORY: <RUN_ROOT>/starrc/star_coupled_Cnom_model_25
EXTRACTION: RC
NETS: *
NETLIST_FORMAT: SPEF
NETLIST_FILE: outputs/<design>.starrc_coupled.Cnom_model_25.spef
COUPLE_TO_GROUND: NO
COUPLING_ABS_THRESHOLD: 0
COUPLING_REL_THRESHOLD: 0
XREF: NO

* Run:  cd <RUN_ROOT> && StarXtract -clean <this_file>.cmd
* The run_*.sh scripts generate this file per corner and execute it for you.
